# eOn SVN r2549. HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel ljcluster.
# Improved dimer, same stops as eon/develop-ts-lj38-dimer. Memory 20, translation L-BFGS max_move 0.1, max_iterations 3000, converged_force 0.001. Dimer rotation is conjugate gradient, converged_angle 0.1, rotations_max 20, improved true. Potential ljcluster. client_displace_type load. direction.dat is Python random.Random(index). Main random_seed is 1. r2549 does not read energy_weighted, ci_mmf, climbing_image_band_slack, setup_mmf_peaks, or the develop L-BFGS catalog past memory, inverse curvature, max inverse curvature, auto scale, and the two resets. Those keys are omitted. The keys it does read sit in [Optimizer]. The run swaps the potential for ext_pot. The harness kernel is the develop kernel for this potential name. The 2014 table used r2156. The binary is SVN r2549, the registry pin. Export of the 2014 revision is forbidden, so this row is r2549.
# Each start is the mean of 2 replicates (svn-all and fortran). n is the number of distinct starts. 0 starts differ in force_calls. Success agrees on every start.
counter harness
code Eon svn
code_version r2549
commit r2549
algorithm LBFGS
tuning default
template eon-svn/ts-lj38-dimer
problem tsopt/LJ38
reducer harness
cap 10000
n 200
par2_mean 644.135
nfailed 1
mean_calls 548.34
median_calls 360.5
min_calls 93.0
max_calls 6078.0
n_crash 0
n_divergence 1
n_cap 0
n_wrong_stationary 0
n_replicates 2
n_differing 0
success_rate 0.995
wilson_low 0.9722262956021069
wilson_high 0.9991168312843989
